#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0288-A expect=skipped domain=TS
#note "THE TSVAL ALL-FACET GATE, INHERITED FROM THE PARENT AT THE R-5.25 SPLIT AND NOW LOAD-BEARING HERE. The split moved the flood risk onto this half: its Check is `empty(TSVAL) and empty(TSVALNF)`, two bare empty leaves, so on a TS dataset with no TSVAL column every row where TSVALNF is also blank would fire (absent = all-missing, EC-43). Requirements.Variables.All [TSVAL] rejects the dataset instead, naming TSVAL. TSVAL is Expected in SENDIG, so an absent column is still reported once by the Expected-variable presence rule -- R-4.11b bucket 2, not a lost signal. If this scenario EXECUTES, the gate has been removed: escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVALNF  type=Char label="Parameter Value Null Flavor"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | STSTDTC | Study Start Date |
S1 | TS | 2 | SPECIES | Species | NA
